1.	Conditional Execution
    a.	Create five well-named Variables.  To each Variable, assign one—and only one—of the following strings: Critical, High, Medium, Low, and Informational.
    b.	Create a well-named Variable (i.e., memory location) of a Float data type and assign any number between 0.0 and 10.0.
    c.	If the Float is within the range 9.0 to 10.0, print “Critical”.
    d.	If the Float is within the range 7.0 to 8.9, print “High”.
    e.	If the Float is within the range 4.0 to 6.9, print “Medium”.
    f.	If the Float is within the range 0.1 to 3.9, print “Low”.
    g.	If the float is 0.0, print “None”.
